# QA M5 (D-075: the scroll moves only in frames of play, not paused):
# a pause in the middle of the auto-scroll changes nothing but the frame
# numbers. Title flow (START at 20, intro until 170, play from 171), then
# the inputs of wolfgangsee_checkpoint with a 302-frame pause inserted
# after its first 1200 frames of play (frame 1371: she swims at the right
# clamp past the Gschwendt pier, camera x ~948): START pauses, 300
# frames idle, START resumes. Everything after it is
# wolfgangsee_checkpoint shifted by exactly 171 + 302 = 473 frames: the
# Gelse #1 sting at 2277 + 473 = 2750, the respawn on the pontoon, the
# 60-frame hold (the title flow adds the 150-frame stage intro after the
# death), the M-box and the Mozartkugel (power big, x >= 2090).
# If the scroll, the push, the timer or any entity moved during the
# pause, the death frame would differ.
